      "side": 1,
      "message": "I’m concerned about shading Bouncy Castle. BC provider JARs are signed, and shading/repackaging typically invalidates or strips those signatures.\n\nSince this is a security provider, that could lead to runtime issues or weaken trust guarantees.\n\nI’d prefer keeping it as a normal runtime dependency rather than embedding it into the shaded standalone JAR.\n\nDo we know how this worked before the migration to Bazel modules? Previously we used PLUGIN_API, which didn’t include Bouncy Castle—so I assume it was either provided by Gerrit itself or not required at runtime in this way.\n\nAs an alternative, could we move this from a standalone utility into a plugin init step? That would allow running it before Gerrit starts and avoid the need for a separate shaded binary. Bouncy Castle is already included in gerrit.war, so we might be able to rely on that instead.\n\nFor example, similar to how the OAuth plugin defines:\n```python\n\"Gerrit-InitStep: com.googlesource.gerrit.plugins.oauth.InitOAuth\",\n```\n\nIf that approach doesn’t work, a simpler fallback might be to provide a small wrapper script instead of shading BC into the binary.",
